<title>MEXICO: Mexico livestock report, feeder export price - USDA.</title>
<headline>Mexico livestock report, feeder export price - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported Tuesday that around 2,000 head were exported into the United States at one crossing point on Monday.</p>
<p>Through Santa Teresa, New Mexico, around 2,000 steer calves and yearlings sold 2-3 cents/lb higher than last week. &quot;Trade moderate, demand good. Bulk of supply consisted of steers weighing 300-600 lb,&quot; the USDA said.</p>
<p>Prices for 300-400 lb feeder steers were between 85-95 cents/lb, for 400-500 lb head they were between 75-85 cents/lb and for 500-600 lb head between 75-80 cents/lb.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com))</p>
